{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css flex basis css flex basis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md","fileName":"CSS Flex Basis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Flex Basis","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CSS Flexible Box Layout]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Flexible Box Layout","CSS Flex Grow and Shrink","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css flex basis css flex basis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md","fileName":"CSS Flex Basis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Flex Basis","heading":"CSS Flex Basis","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The `flex-basis` property establishes an item's starting main-axis size before [[CSS Flex Grow and Shrink|growth or shrinkage]] distributes free space. It can use a length, percentage, content-based value, or `auto` behavior that consults the relevant width or height.\n\nA zero basis asks items to divide space mainly according to flex factors, whereas an automatic or content basis preserves more of their starting size. The `flex` shorthand combines basis, growth, and shrink factors.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Flexible Box Layout","CSS Flex Grow and Shrink","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css flex basis css flex basis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Flex Basis.md","fileName":"CSS F